STAGED PATCH 0004 (kernel round) of 5: apply after 0001.
Target: Linux 6.12.116, mm/vmalloc.c. Line anchors are
the manifest's numbers of record, checked against the
pristine tree; context lines are schematic. Re-base
on the real tree before applying.

Subject: iscandar: vmalloc backing at 2.3, free doors
at 2.4, in kernel form

The family splits at its own seam, as the bridge
staging had it: the reservation half (2.2,
__get_vm_area_node and alloc_vmap_area) stays stock,
address-space bookkeeping that was never part of the
replacement, and is not patched. Only the backing is
replaced: where the stock body fills the area's page
array page by page from the page allocator, the core
serves ONE exact-fit run for the whole area, and the
array is filled with the run's frames in order,
through the core's own offset-to-page conversion.

One vmalloc contains a hidden slab allocation (the
page-pointer array, allocated by a recursive vmalloc
call into Family 1): it arrives at 1.1 as any cache
allocation does, and the books expect vmalloc traffic
to touch Family 1 in this way. Unchanged from the
bridge round.

The bridge staging left one question open at
vfree_atomic, in its own words: whether the atomic
door could take the same record "is not pre-decided."
This build decides it. The core's free path is
sleep-free inside its irqsave section, so an atomic
caller is served exactly as a process-context caller
is (design section 3: atomic-context callers, which
the bridge refused, are served). vfree_atomic takes
the same range decision and the same door as vfree.

--- a/mm/vmalloc.c
+++ b/mm/vmalloc.c
@@ -3594,7 +3594,25 @@
-static int vm_area_alloc_pages(...)
+static int vm_area_alloc_pages(...)
 {
+	if (iscandar_active()) {
+		void *run;
+		unsigned int i;
+
+		run = iscandar_alloc((u64)area->nr_pages << PAGE_SHIFT,
+				     PAGE_SIZE, 0);
+		if (!run)
+			return -ENOMEM;
+		for (i = 0; i < area->nr_pages; i++)
+			area->pages[i] = iscandar_offset_to_page(
+				iscandar_ptr_to_offset(run)
+				+ ((u64)i << PAGE_SHIFT));
+		return 0;
+	}
+	iscandar_prefix_note(ISCANDAR_CENTER_VMALLOC_BACKING,
+			     (size_t)area->nr_pages << PAGE_SHIFT);
 	...
 }
@@ -3407,6 +3425,12 @@
-void vfree(const void *addr)
+void vfree(const void *addr)
 {
+	if (iscandar_ptr_in_arena(addr)) {
+		iscandar_free(addr, 0);
+		return;
+	}
 	...
 }
@@ -3373,4 +3397,14 @@
-void vfree_atomic(const void *addr)
+void vfree_atomic(const void *addr)
 {
+	/* The same door as vfree, taken in this build: the
+	 * core's free path does not sleep, so the atomic
+	 * caller's contract is met by the same range
+	 * decision and the same call. */
+	if (iscandar_ptr_in_arena(addr)) {
+		iscandar_free(addr, 0);
+		return;
+	}
 	...
 }
